<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frösö Runestone</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Frösöstenen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Frösö Runestone is an 11th-century runestone on the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/froson">Frösön</a> in Jämtland, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, and the northernmost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viking-age">Viking Age</a> runestone in the country. Its inscription states that Östman, son of Gudfast, raised the stone, built a bridge and had Jämtland Christianised, making it a rare record of the region's conversion.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/froso-runestone.jpg" alt="Frösö Runestone" width="320" height="651" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andreaze · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fr%C3%B6s%C3%B6stenen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
